And Flash, Beauty Queen Riot. Contestants sue each other.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:08.720
Yeah, we got some great pictures, but Jeff says we're a family newspaper.

00:05:08.900 --> 00:05:11.370
Down here, Mr. Davis. Anything new on the test?

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:15.850
Only the last AP report, sir. New York announced it was detonated 25 miles from the South Pole.

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:16.990
Must be the biggest bang yet.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.150
Not the test of cricket.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:19.730
Oh, sorry, sir.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.100
Still no play.

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:22.300
Were you getting tea?

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:23.920
I wasn't, Mr. Davis.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:24.660
Well, you are now.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:26.250
Anything else exciting?

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:29.830
Yeah, four transatlantic jets grounded with reported navigation trouble.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.340
Of course there's navigation trouble.

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:32.220
Sunspots.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:32.980
Sunspots?

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.200
Well, that's a silly question.

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:35.940
All right here, Mr. McGuire.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:37.860
More protest letters, sir.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.200
Oh, no, take them to Features.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:40.800
Features, sir, take them to you, sir.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:43.100
I can't stop the bloody bomb.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:44.300
It went off ten days ago.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:45.460
All right, put them down.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:48.140
Take those back to the mall, will you, sir?

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:51.860
Yeah, no, this is Bill McGuire here.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:55.170
Oh, I'm sorry, Sandy, he's out of the office at the moment.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.140
Oh, yes, even reporters have to go sometimes.

00:05:59.500 --> 00:05:59.920
Yes, all right.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.850
tell him would you mind telling me something i was under the impression that you wanted a piece

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:07.670
on thrombosis well as i can only do one thing at a time what am i expected to do with all these

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:13.250
protest letters thank you very much but there's 1700 of them don't worry about that now go down

00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:16.850
and see if my car's back will you it's a tan morrison the side entrance if it is mr stenning's

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:21.250
probably in harry's bar telling me he's wanted quick sir and how is the thrombosis market great

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:26.360
this will give the higher paid executive readers a nice moment of anxiety at their breakfast tomorrow

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:26.980
Boy!

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:44.240
Mr. Sanderson's asking for you, Mr. Stenning.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.050
So they sent Pip the cabin boy to bail me out.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:48.520
I think he was in a hurry, sir.

00:06:48.580 --> 00:06:50.680
Yes, well, you just tell him I'll be coming up when he sees the bubbles.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:53.320
I've just got to get some clips in the library, sir.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:54.760
Fine, make sure my picture is up to date.

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:56.360
But why all to my heading?

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:57.760
What's he trying to do, make a job for himself?

00:06:57.880 --> 00:06:59.960
Bill, you can't print a picture on thrombosis, isn't it?

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.920
call it you two can be the death of the party. No, we're all getting soft. That's what we're all

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:09.880
getting, soft. Hi, Billy Boy. Good evening. Well, your car's safely back. It's a fine vessel and should

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:14.440
prove seaworthy for another hundred years or so. What I don't understand, why bother to come back?

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:21.160
You borrow my car for lunch, why bother to hurry back at 6.30? I saw my kid today. Oh, yeah? Yeah,

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:25.210
Ballacy Pleasure Gardens. She lets me see him sometimes. It's my legal right, you know.

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:29.920
We spent the afternoon on the ghost train. The only customers in the rain.

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:32.090
You know, Sandy's been screaming for years.

00:07:32.170 --> 00:07:32.950
He's a nice little kid.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:34.490
Bright, too.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:36.620
Remembered me after about ten minutes.

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:41.030
You can throw this lot down, too.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:41.790
My floor's full.

00:07:42.010 --> 00:07:43.780
Oh, what's it like to have fan mail?

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:47.220
The biggest experimental bang of all time is ten days old.

00:07:47.340 --> 00:07:49.200
Instead of being proud, the public demands we stop it.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:49.760
Oh, I don't know.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:52.620
The best science man in the street ought to be able to pull off a little job like that.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:53.800
Make a trick film, maybe.

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:54.960
Yeah, you know.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:07:56.580
The mushroom goes back into the bomb.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.980
The bomb goes back into the plane, which flies backwards over the task force, steaming back...

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:03.920
We'd better start climbing backwards to Sandy's office, he wouldn't believe you're insured.

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:07.780
He probably wants me to take over the science desk. Promotion. Stenning rises again.

00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:10.800
Don't think you wouldn't be welcome. What have we got?

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:14.290
A flash. Spitzbergen reports the largest earth tremors ever recorded.

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:17.210
Sorry I wasn't around, Sandy.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.960
Okay, I'm used to it. Do you know anything about sunspots?

00:08:21.080 --> 00:08:25.210
Sunspots? Do you hear that static?

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:27.550
My favourite tune, but I don't think it'll make the top ten.

00:08:27.790 --> 00:08:29.960
I'm not joking, Pete. There's usually a lot of sunspots.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:32.700
If you're enjoying the last week, it's been heavier than ever.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:34.600
The TV people are having trouble with their pictures.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:35.300
Yeah, so's the public.

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:37.670
Do me a 500-worder for the leader page.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:38.090
Success!

00:08:38.750 --> 00:08:41.790
Wait a minute. Here are a couple of items about navigation trouble.

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:42.990
Maybe you can tie them in.

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:43.430
Yeah, why not?

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:46.320
Hey, great idea!

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:48.950
With all these floods, what about a daily express arc?

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:50.380
Great sales promotion, Sandy.

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:51.350
You know what, Pete?

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:53.320
I really think you're gonna have to try a bit harder.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:55.100
This paper isn't built to carry passengers.

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:57.540
All right.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.470
Well, Billy Boy, they've got me doing your homework.

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:07.950
500 words on sunspots.

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:09.810
Have you seen the figures on some of these Earth-premises?

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:11.510
Here's another planet trying to contact us.

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.150
Are you receiving me? Are you receiving me?

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:14.190
You are? We'll get knotted.

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:16.970
Must have been a hell of a big bang to give these seismograph readings.

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:18.450
Tell me all about sunspots, Daddy.

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:23.560
Sunspots are caused when the rays of the sun beat down on an unprotected torso,

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:25.940
thus causing a sun rash similar to acne.

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:27.880
I thought it was clean living that did that.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:29.980
Bring up the meteorological center, see if we can speak to Sir...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.360
John Kelly, maybe he'll give us some quotes.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.020
If not, you can talk to Pat Holroyd.

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:34.780
Pat Holroyd, that bloke from Picture Post.

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:36.580
Oh, he's P.R.O. now. He's gone legitimate.

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:39.170
Wow. This calls for a celebration toast.

00:09:39.390 --> 00:09:41.280
Pete, bring the med center.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:44.220
I'll be back. It's six and a half minutes past my medicine time.

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:46.110
Get me the med center, please.

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:55.230
Thanks for holding on, Bill.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:56.400
Holding on to what?

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:59.070
My job. This may not be a revelation to you, but...

00:09:59.070 --> 00:09:59.790
And I quote the...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.220
It's just gone, but it's really gone.

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:02.300
You know what I think?

00:10:02.440 --> 00:10:04.140
I should get my finger out and back on the typewriter.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:04.820
Roughly.

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:06.380
Alcoholics of the press unite.

00:10:08.760 --> 00:10:09.040
Yes?

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:10.170
Oh, yes.

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:12.140
This is Peter Stenning, Daily Express.

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:13.080
Sir John Kelly, please.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:15.300
Well, it's nice of you to be interested.

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:16.780
I want to speak about sunspots.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.030
Just one moment, please.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:18.990
What do I do with the press?

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:20.050
What does he want you to do?

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:22.280
I want to talk to Sir John about sunspots.

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:22.860
Oh, dreary.

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:23.500
Press office.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:24.700
No direct calls to Sir John.

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:25.740
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:26.960
I'm putting you through the press office.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:29.090
Look, I don't want the press office, dear.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:29.970
I want Sir John Kelly...

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.100
All right, all right, then get me Mr. Pat Holroyd.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:36.380
Yeah. Oh, yes, Sandy.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:39.760
Yes, I understand all that, dear, but Holroyd knows me.

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:40.780
The readings do be this big at that distance.

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:42.560
Now, just tell him Peter Stenning.

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.480
No, I'd rather do this myself.

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:45.800
I've got my own sources.

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:47.720
Look, just tell Mr. Holroyd.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:49.160
This girl's a bigger threat than radiation.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:50.650
I heard that remark.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.670
Listen, I don't care if you're Lord Rothermere himself.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:54.230
All right, Beaverbrook.

00:10:54.370 --> 00:10:55.770
I'm putting you through to the press office.

00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:57.290
You were going to get me Mr. Holroyd.

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:59.530
Would you get me Professor Lambert, Aldermaster...

00:10:59.530 --> 00:10:59.970
Listen, you're...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.060
Your job is to pass messages on when you're asked.

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:05.120
My job is to do what I'm told by the people who gave me the job.

00:11:05.180 --> 00:11:07.240
In any way, this isn't my job. I'm from the pool.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:09.000
Well, why don't you dive back in and drown?

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:12.000
I take it. You didn't get much change out of her.

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:15.740
I'm going over there, and I'm going to shake her till the tilt sign goes up.

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:17.960
Fine. In the meantime, shake my car keys out of your pocket.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:19.560
I may want to use it before closing time.

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:22.570
Hello, Professor Lambert.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:26.580
Hello, it's Bill Maguire here, Daily Express, Tom.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:27.760
Hello.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:29.970
Tom, about the side...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.100
Asmograph readings of the latest American experiment.

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:36.090
Would you say they were bigger than the official announcement gives out?

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:38.560
Well, off the record, of course.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:42.240
Something pretty huge, huh?

00:11:57.830 --> 00:11:58.270
Next office.

00:11:58.640 --> 00:11:59.480
Trade through, second left.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:01.780
Mr. Holroyd's on the same floor, isn't he?

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:02.780
No, sir. One up.

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:03.830
Did you have an appointment?

00:12:03.890 --> 00:12:05.350
No, I'm just going into the press office.

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:24.180
This is a bit better than picture post, isn't it?

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:25.600
Tenning, what the hell do you want?

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:27.000
A quote on sunspots.

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:27.520
Sunspots?

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:29.960
Look, just tell me that the static, the monsoon, the...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.920
compass trouble and the terrible shows we get on television are all caused by sunspots

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:37.290
and that the sunspots are caused by bigger bomb experiments and I'll leave you in peace.

00:12:37.450 --> 00:12:40.970
Well, there usually is a bit of extra sunspot activity this time of year, old boy,

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:42.350
but I don't think it has much to do with anything.

00:12:42.370 --> 00:12:43.270
But there could be some connection.

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:44.970
Oh, come on, say yes.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:45.830
Well, how could it do you?

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:48.990
Look, Stenny, it's nice to see you again, but I'm afraid I'm up to my neck, old boy.

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:52.420
All right, Miss Johnson, take this to the typing pool, have it mimeographed immediately.

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:55.950
I see you're still a bit of a liberty taker, Stenny.

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:56.950
Well, give me something, Pat.

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:58.150
I've got to get a story out of this.

00:12:58.210 --> 00:12:59.370
Sorry, can't apply, Joe, boy.

00:12:59.470 --> 00:12:59.970
Well, why not?

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.500
It's a perfectly routine, harmless, silly-season story.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:04.520
Look, Peter, no right to be here.

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:05.020
Well, it is, isn't it?

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:07.460
Well, just tell me yes or no.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:09.670
I don't have to tell you anything, Stenny.

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:12.650
No special position that entitles you to a first break

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:14.070
on anything that comes into this office.

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:15.650
You mean something has come in?

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:18.990
Johnson.

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:20.680
She's out of the office, Sir John.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:21.240
Who's that?

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:22.370
All right, sir.

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:23.220
Come in immediately.

00:13:24.580 --> 00:13:27.480
If you don't mind, Stenny.

00:13:27.560 --> 00:13:29.960
I suppose there couldn't be some information that hasn't hit the...

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:33.820
If there is, you'll get it when everyone else does, in the official release.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.820
Oh, Miss Johnson, perhaps you'll take Mr. Stenning down to the press room, would you?

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:38.500
Of course.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:40.540
Nice to meet an old pal.

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:42.300
Come this way, please, Mr. Stenning.

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:46.530
Normally, darling, it would be a pleasure, but at the moment, work before women.

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:50.110
The general pattern is pretty clear, but until we get the full picture, yes.

00:13:50.270 --> 00:13:51.630
Sir John, I've only one question to ask you.

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:51.670
Who are you?

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.810
I think this gentleman's come to the wrong department.

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:56.990
How are the effects of the recent bomb different from all the others we've managed to survive?

00:13:57.090 --> 00:13:59.910
I don't know what your job is, young man, but it's not mine to speculate.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:00.600
Come along.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:02.200
But they are different, aren't they, Sir John?

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:03.500
You're not making it any easier for yourself.

00:14:03.700 --> 00:14:05.160
All right, all right, relax.

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:08.830
Good try, old man, but these diabolical liberties, don't you know?

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:11.170
Oh, come of it. You've gatecrashed for a story often enough.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:26.320
Oh, hello. Have you come to fix this?

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:27.700
Well, I hadn't, but for you, why not?

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:29.890
Oh, I'm sorry. They said they'd send someone.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.460
Can I help you? Nearly everyone's gone home.

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:34.320
Yeah, I'd like a copy of tonight's official lie release.

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:35.480
Tonight's what?

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:37.090
The official release, sweetie.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:39.200
Oh, those are all a bit smudged.

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.420
It's over-inking. I'll get you a clean one.

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:44.290
We're in a terrible state here.

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:47.290
What with summer holidays and flu, we're all doing everyone else's job.

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:48.250
